Mobile tmux trials exposed a frozen planning timer, clipped controls,
ambiguous activity messages, expensive planning commands, and planner
responses wrapped in prose. The dashboard now separates controller state
from observed agent activity and keeps controls visible in small panes.
Claude planning exposes only inspection tools. Planning has no timeout,
as requested. Go is the default; the Bash file only launches Go.

Validation: make test, make race, and the four Measuretwice adapter tests
using the documented local module path. Earlier tmux checks covered
58x24, 40x18, and 30x12 panes. The actual failed planner response was
replayed through parsing and plan validation without modifying Margin.
